 891:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****         /* Priority grouping:  The interrupt controller (NVIC) allows the bits
 892:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****          * that define each interrupt's priority to be split between bits that
 893:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****          * define the interrupt's pre-emption priority bits and bits that define
 894:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****          * the interrupt's sub-priority.  For simplicity all bits must be defined
 895:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****          * to be pre-emption priority bits.  The following assertion will fail if
 896:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****          * this is not the case (if some bits represent a sub-priority).
 897:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****          *
 898:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****          * If the application only uses CMSIS libraries for interrupt
